## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-vehicles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Search by plate, model or owner. <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates for many cars</b> changes the rates of many cars at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.3%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.5%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:52.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-set-a-car-s-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Set a car&#39;s rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then the <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Kilometres: keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car&#39;s class), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b> and type them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rate</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily rate</td><td>A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday</td></tr><tr><td>Weekend rate</td><td>A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly rate</td><td>The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rate</td><td>The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tiers there), <b class="gd-ui">Off for this car</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Its own tiers</b> (a table like the one in Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fleet-tracking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet tracking</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> tab. Fleet staff have the same map as <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b> in their menu, and field staff see the cars of their own jobs under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. Positions are seen by Admins and fleet staff only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car&#39;s power, and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b>: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b> to see where, <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> when it is handled, or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Trips by booking</b>: each booking&#39;s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pair-a-tracker-with-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pair a tracker with a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A new tracker that reports shows under <b class="gd-ui">Trackers</b>, &quot;Reporting, not on a car yet&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Pair</b>, choose the car and the install date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Pair a tracker</b> and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner&#39;s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car&#39;s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a tracker off a car (tick &quot;faulty&quot; for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracking-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracking settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before &quot;not reporting&quot; (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car&#39;s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA&#39;s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the ingest key</b>: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), <b class="gd-ui">2 Cover plates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 Review</b> and <b class="gd-ui">4 Live on the site</b>. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with <b class="gd-ui">Retry</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">On each public photo press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b>. The editor opens.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The box over the plate is already suggested: as soon as the review opens, every outside photo (the More outside photos included) gets its suggestion, and those photos show Box suggested. Check it. <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under Cover the plate with, choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-photos-filed-under-the-wrong-shot-and-interior-windows" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing&#39;s photos change in the review instead (Reject).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-out and check-in photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings &gt; Usage counts them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner, documents, tracker</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pickup-from-owner-and-return-to-owner-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> records the car&#39;s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car&#39;s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'owner-money', 'chapter', 'owners-and-onboarding', 'Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.

## Owner invoices

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Invoices** tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner''s and each application''s Invoices tab.

1. Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.
2. **New invoice** makes an invoice of any amount for an owner''s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.
3. The monthly run and tracker invoices: **Run the monthly invoices** issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); **Issue all tracker invoices** bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.

![](/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1060; address: carmacars.ca/admin/invoices; pins: 1 83.3 22.4, 2 41.7 35.7, 3 29.0 43.4")

## Make, edit and issue an invoice

A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.

1. Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. **Add a line** for more.
2. **Save as draft** to come back to it, or **Save and issue** to send it now. On a draft''s page, **Issue and email** sends it.
3. Paid another way? Press **Record payment** on the invoice. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.
4. **Resend email** sends the invoice again. **PDF** opens it as a PDF.

## Correct an issued invoice

An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.

1. Press **Void**, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press **Void the invoice**. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.
2. The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press **Save and issue**.
3. Already paid? Void the payment first, or press **Credit note** for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.

Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.

## The automatic debit

The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for returned debits and owners without a mandate.

:::flow
Notice day | Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before
Debit day | The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice
Cleared | The invoice is paid
Returned, insufficient funds | The $50.00 Late Fee is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days
Returned for another reason | No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task
:::

1. The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.
2. How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.
3. Scheduled and processing lists each debit. **Pause** holds one (a reason is needed).
4. Owners lists each mandate. Use **Pause**, **Resume** or **Send a notice now**.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 920; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 1 21.8 21.7, 2 21.5 35.5, 3 91.5 75.4, 4 84.7 94.7")

5. Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank''s reason.
6. Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.
7. Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 5 11.0 14.4, 6 10.2 52.3, 7 15.4 89.8")

Insufficient funds: the $50.00 Late Fee is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner''s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task.

> Watch out: Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner''s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no mandate gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.

## Owner statements

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Statements** tab

1. Press **Build all for a month** (or **Build one**).
2. Open each draft. Check it, **Rebuild** after a correction, **Preview PDF**, then **Approve**.
3. Press **Issue to the owner**. **Reissue** sends a corrected copy; **CSV** exports it.

![](/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 400; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements; pins: 1 79.9 27.3")

![An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.](/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000; pins: 3 86.0 22.7")

## Staff commissions

**Money** > **Company**, the **Commissions** tab. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Not earned yet | The rental is ahead, or not paid in full
Pending approval | Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended
Approved | You approved it; the staff member is told
Paid | You recorded the payment; the staff member is told
Reversed | Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment
:::

1. By person shows each staff member''s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.
2. Press **Approve** on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.
3. Press **Record a payment**: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.
4. **Prices to review** lists prices typed by hand; **Sourcing claims** lists staff who say they sourced a website request; **Payments made** lists each payment.
5. **Owner requests** lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company''s share or of the cars'' rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press **Approve**, **Change and approve** (your terms, with a note) or **Decline**. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner''s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner''s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.
6. Who sourced an owner: the owner''s page, **Sourced by**. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.

|  | Commission |
| --- | --- |
| Sales | By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month''s rentals |
| An owner a salesperson brought in | The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars'', a partner''s or a shareholder''s cars |
| Customer service, finance, fleet, field staff | 10% (also the field referral fee) |
| Base | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off |
| On the owner statement | An owner''s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner''s car: from CarmaCars'' commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense |

> Tip: A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month''s Sales tier) goes on the owner''s next statement as an adjustment line.

## Field pay

**Money** > **Company**, the **Field pay** tab. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Clocked in and out | Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out
Pay run started | Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions
Approved | The figures are frozen, the period''s hours are locked, the statements are numbered
Paid | You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email
:::

1. The tab **Pay run** shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings > Program, Field pay). **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between periods.
2. After the period ends, press **Start the pay run**: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). **Refresh the figures** takes in a change made since.
3. Press **Approve**. The period''s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under **Hours** first. **Withdraw** takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.
4. Press **Record payment** on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (**Send again** repeats it). The statement''s number opens its PDF; **CSV** gives the run for your accountant.
5. **Hours** lists everyone''s shifts of the period. **Add hours** enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.
6. **Hourly rates** shows each person''s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with **Set the rate** (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.

|  | Field pay |
| --- | --- |
| Overtime | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate |
| Vacation pay | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement |
| Deductions | None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer''s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so |
| Commissions that net to nothing | A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next |

> Tip: A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.

## Company model

Money > **Company model** is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.

1. **Forecast**: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months'' EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.
2. **Actuals**: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental''s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. **Refresh actuals now** recomputes them at once.
3. **Pro forma 5 years**: each year''s income statement, cash flow and key figures.
4. **Assumptions**: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press **Save the assumptions**; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked "From the actuals" left blank uses the latest complete month.
5. **Download as Excel**: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.

> Tip: Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month''s costs in Money > Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.

## Company statements

**Money** > **Company**, the **Monthly statements** tab: CarmaCars'' own monthly statement, in twelve sections.

1. Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.
2. Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.
3. Download **PDF**, **PDF by owner** or **PDF by vehicle**, or press **Email me the PDFs**.
4. **Finalize** freezes the month. **Rebuild** works until then.

![](/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/reports; pins: 1 20.8 28.0, 2 19.4 59.3, 3 77.1 15.5, 4 46.9 15.5")

### Fees taken from the revenue statement
On an owner''s page, the **Fees** button sets **How fees are paid**: **Bank debit** (the default) or **Take from revenue statement**. Taken from the statement, the owner''s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement". Approved, the invoice reads **Paid from statement**, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task **Invoice ... back to the bank debit**.

### The flat-rate agreements
An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement** instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner''s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings > **Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK** is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.

## How it''s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts

Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: **Bank debit on the 15th**, or **Deduct from payouts** (taken from the owner''s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).

1. On an invoice, **How it''s paid**, **Change**. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.
2. Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.
3. For the first and last month, choose **Deduct from payouts** on the Terms tab (or at approval).
4. On the Terms tab, **Charge the agreed one-off fees** makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner''s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.
', 'Owner money', 'Owner invoices (drafts, void and reissue, credit notes), the automatic debit, statements, payouts and the company statement.',
