## On one screen (release 28)

On the booking page the check-out is one screen: the time, km, fuel, and many photos picked at once from the camera roll, with the suggested angles as a checklist. If the renter checked in themselves, add your photos to theirs. The full checklist is still there when you want it.',
  '<p class="gd-p">You give the renter the keys only after every check passes. The steps guide you one by one: press Next after each, Back to go back.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The job&#39;s header shows how much of the rental walkthrough the renter has read, for example &quot;Renter&#39;s walkthrough: read 2 of 6 steps&quot;. Below 6, walk them through the rest at the car: what to bring, the walk-around, the road rules and the return.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Finish the handover in the app, to the last step. Until the pickup is recorded the renter&#39;s messages and the office&#39;s records are guesses: 30 minutes after the pickup time you get an alert and a text to record it, or to mark a no-show.</div></aside><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-before-you-start-the-ready-check" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Before you start: the ready check</h2><p class="gd-p">The first step lists what must be done before the car can go: signed, paid, ID checked, deposit.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each line should show a green tick: agreement signed, identity verified, coverage confirmed, additional drivers accepted, the booking holds the calendar, deposit taken.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A red line shows what you can do about it right under it (see the next part). Fix it, then press <b class="gd-ui">Check again</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">All green? Press <b class="gd-ui">Next</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Coverage or the calendar not ready? Only the office fixes those: call CarmaCars. Still not ready? Press <b class="gd-ui">Stop: do not release the car</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/410"><img src="/guides/img/field-21-handover-01-ready-phone-ecb54c56.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="410"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91%;top:63.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Never hand over keys if the ready check fails, the renter does not match the photo on file, or they do not have their original licence or the card on file. Stop and call us.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-fix-the-ready-check-on-the-spot" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fix the ready check on the spot</h2><p class="gd-p">Most red lines are fixed on your phone, without calling the office. Everything you do is recorded with your name.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Agreement not signed: press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b> and hand the phone to the renter. Signed on paper instead? Open <b class="gd-ui">Signed on paper instead? Scan it</b>, take a photo of each page, then press <b class="gd-ui">Record the signed paper copy</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Identity not verified: for each driver, press <b class="gd-ui">Take</b> for the licence front, the back and the selfie. Hold the original licence: tick that the name matches, the photo is the person, it is valid past the return and it is class G2 or G. No expiry on file? Type the licence number and the expiry. Press <b class="gd-ui">The licence checks out</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Deposit not taken: press <b class="gd-ui">Card hold: hand this phone to the renter</b>. They type their card in Stripe&#39;s secure form; take the phone back and press <b class="gd-ui">Back to the job</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Paid by e-Transfer instead: open <b class="gd-ui">Paid by e-Transfer</b>, type the reference number from their confirmation and press <b class="gd-ui">Record the e-Transfer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Paid in cash: open <b class="gd-ui">Paid in cash</b>, count the amount in front of the renter and press <b class="gd-ui">I received</b>. Keep the cash apart from your own money and hand it to CarmaCars within 1 business day, as Finance directs: Finance gets a task to collect it from you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Additional driver not accepted: press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device (additional driver)</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An expired licence, a face that does not match or a renter who will not sign: do not fix it. Press Stop and call us.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-the-steps-one-by-one" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The steps, one by one</h2><div class="gd-phones"><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div>Car ready: fuel full or charged 80%, clean, extras in. <b class="gd-ui">Yes</b> or <b class="gd-ui">No</b>, with a note for Fleet.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-22-handover-02-car-ready-phone-c118e08b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div>Is this the renter? Compare the person with the name and photo on file.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-23-handover-03-renter-phone-813b8ced.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div>Original licence: name, photo and expiry match. A photo of a licence is not enough.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-24-handover-04-licence-phone-80a47254.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div>Card on File: you have seen the physical card with the same last four digits, in the renter&#39;s name.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-25-handover-05-card-phone-64652ced.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div>Odometer: type the reading in km.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-26-handover-06-odometer-phone-34c4cbd7.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div>Fuel or charge: tap the level on the gauge, in eighths from E to F.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-27-handover-07-fuel-phone-2df75f41.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div></div><div class="gd-phones"><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div>Keys: how many keys and fobs you hand over. Use <b class="gd-ui">+</b> and <b class="gd-ui">−</b>.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-28-handover-08-keys-phone-13bec781.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div>Photo set: 19 photos in order. Press <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> for the next one; every photo is also in the list below, with <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> if needed.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-29-handover-09-photos-phone-767ecd4f.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div>Damage: tap the car diagram where it is, choose Where and Type, then <b class="gd-ui">Add the damage</b>.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-30-handover-10-damage-phone-a43b142f.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div>Tracker: it should say in place and reporting. <b class="gd-ui">Check again</b> if not. The car has to go anyway? Open <b class="gd-ui">The car has to go anyway?</b>, say why and press <b class="gd-ui">Release without the tracker</b>: an Admin is told at once.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-31-handover-11-tracker-phone-817976ce.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div>Renter reviews: the renter reads the summary of odometer, fuel, keys, photos and damage.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-32-handover-12-summary-phone-b1787a2d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-pcell"><div class="gd-pcap"><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div>Signatures: the renter signs, then you. <b class="gd-ui">Use this signature</b> for each.</div></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/350"><img src="/guides/img/field-33-handover-13-signatures-phone-fac8ea8d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="350"></div></div></figure></div></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="13"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b>. You see &quot;Checked out. The rental has started.&quot; The renter gets the photo report by email and in their Documents.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Photos wait on the phone without a connection and upload by themselves when it returns; the count shows what is still uploading. Each photo keeps its time, and the place when your phone allows location. No signal on a step? It says &quot;Answers kept on this phone&quot; and you can go on: press Try again, or they are sent when the signal returns.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-sign-now-on-this-device" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign now on this device</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter (or an additional driver) has not signed the rental agreement yet? They sign on your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the job, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>. It shows who still has to sign and whether their licence is on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the person: the name matches their licence, and you saw the original licence. Tick both. No licence on file? Press <b class="gd-ui">Photograph: Licence, front</b> (and the back and the selfie).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> and their name. They read the agreements (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), tick the statements and sign with their name or their finger.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">They hand the phone back: press <b class="gd-ui">Back to the staff view</b>. The signature record says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your phone.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-the-agreements-at-check-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The agreements at check-out</h2><p class="gd-p">Both rental agreements follow the check-out.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Signing at pickup? Record the odometer and the fuel on the check-out first, then hand over the device: the agreement then shows the time, kilometres and fuel out, and the signed copy holds them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The signer gets a code on their phone, initials the key terms, ticks the consents and draws their signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Already signed online? When you complete the check-out, the &quot;as picked up&quot; copy of both agreements is made with your readings and your countersignature, and emailed to the renter.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The check-out stops if the agreement is missing something a claim needs (a licence expiry, a VIN). Ask the office to fill it on the booking, or an Admin to override.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-the-deposit-on-your-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The deposit on your phone</h2><p class="gd-p">Deposit not taken yet? The ready check shows how to take it under the Deposit line. You never type a card number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Card hold: hand this phone to the renter</b>. They type their credit card in Stripe&#39;s secure form and press the button with the amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They see &quot;Hold placed&quot;: take the phone back and press <b class="gd-ui">Back to the job</b>. The ready check shows the deposit taken.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A rental longer than the hold limit shows <b class="gd-ui">Save the card on this phone (long rental)</b> instead: Finance charges the deposit to that card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">No credit card? When CarmaCars allows it, the renter pays the deposit by e-Transfer or in cash: record it under the Deposit line.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-add-ons-to-put-in-the-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add-ons to put in the car</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking may come with add-ons: a baby seat, a child or booster seat, flowers, an umbrella, a phone charger or a prepaid full tank.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the job. Under Put in the car you see each add-on, how many, and what to do (for example &quot;Put the bouquet on the front passenger seat&quot;).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Put every item in the car before the handover. The Car ready step lists them again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Prepaid fuel: the renter may return the car at any fuel level. Do not charge for fuel at the return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A chauffeur on the booking: Fleet tells you who drives and when.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An item missing? Write it in the note for Fleet on the Car ready step and call the office before the handover.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The photo count shows &quot;19 of 19 photos taken · all uploaded&quot; when the set is complete. The first photo must show the plate. Open circles on the damage diagram were recorded before; add only what is new.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-handover-on-one-screen-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">On one screen (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page the check-out is one screen: the time, km, fuel, and many photos picked at once from the camera roll, with the suggested angles as a checklist. If the renter checked in themselves, add your photos to theirs. The full checklist is still there when you want it.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'a-return', 'chapter', 'a-handover', 'The return mirrors the handover. You record the car as it comes back and compare it with the pickup.

## Take the car back

1. Car and keys received: confirm you have the car and its keys.
2. Odometer, then Fuel or charge, as at pickup.
3. Keys and extras: count what came back.
4. Cleanliness: inside and out.
5. Photo set: the same shots, in the same order, as at pickup.
6. Compare with pickup: for new damage, tap the diagram, fill in Where and What it is, press **Add the damage** and take a close-up photo.
7. Belongings: check the seats, the trunk, the glovebox and the door pockets.
8. Renter reviews and signs. Then you sign.
9. Press **Complete the return**. The check-in time is the moment you press it: a late return, the kilometres over the allowance and the fuel or charge used are charged from it automatically. The deposit is not given back at the return: Finance settles it once tolls and tickets have had time to come in (about 7 days), and new damage you mark keeps it held.
10. The closing copy of both rental agreements follows by itself: time and date in, kilometres in, driven and charged, fuel in, the hours late, the new damage, the return charges and the totals, countersigned with your name, emailed to the renter.

> Watch out: New damage needs a close-up photo and a clear note. Finance uses your photos and notes to bill the renter, so take your time.

> Tip: If the renter already pressed I''ve returned the car, the booking shows **The renter says the car is back** with their photos and readings. Check the car in as usual: that completes the trip and settles their report.
', 'A return', 'Odometer, fuel, keys, cleanliness, photos, new damage, belongings and signatures.',
  'The return mirrors the handover. You record the car as it comes back and compare it with the pickup.

## Take the car back

1. Car and keys received: confirm you have the car and its keys.
2. Odometer, then Fuel or charge, as at pickup.
3. Keys and extras: count what came back.
4. Cleanliness: inside and out.
5. Photo set: the same shots, in the same order, as at pickup.
6. Compare with pickup: for new damage, tap the diagram, fill in Where and What it is, press **Add the damage** and take a close-up photo.
7. Belongings: check the seats, the trunk, the glovebox and the door pockets.
8. Renter reviews and signs. Then you sign.
9. Press **Complete the return**. The check-in time is the moment you press it: a late return, the kilometres over the allowance and the fuel or charge used are charged from it automatically. The deposit is not given back at the return: Finance settles it once tolls and tickets have had time to come in (about 7 days), and new damage you mark keeps it held.
10. The closing copy of both rental agreements follows by itself: time and date in, kilometres in, driven and charged, fuel in, the hours late, the new damage, the return charges and the totals, countersigned with your name, emailed to the renter.

> Watch out: New damage needs a close-up photo and a clear note. Finance uses your photos and notes to bill the renter, so take your time.

> Tip: If the renter already pressed I''ve returned the car, the booking shows **The renter says the car is back** with their photos and readings. Check the car in as usual: that completes the trip and settles their report.

## On one screen (release 28)

The check-in is one screen too: the actual return time (late charges follow it), km, fuel, photos and a note. A renter who returned the car themselves with km, fuel and photos has already completed the trip; add photos if anything is missing.',
  '<p class="gd-p">The return mirrors the handover. You record the car as it comes back and compare it with the pickup.</p><section class="gd-task" id="a-return-take-the-car-back" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take the car back</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Car and keys received: confirm you have the car and its keys.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Odometer, then Fuel or charge, as at pickup.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Keys and extras: count what came back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cleanliness: inside and out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Photo set: the same shots, in the same order, as at pickup.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Compare with pickup: for new damage, tap the diagram, fill in Where and What it is, press <b class="gd-ui">Add the damage</b> and take a close-up photo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Belongings: check the seats, the trunk, the glovebox and the door pockets.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Renter reviews and signs. Then you sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>. The check-in time is the moment you press it: a late return, the kilometres over the allowance and the fuel or charge used are charged from it automatically. The deposit is not given back at the return: Finance settles it once tolls and tickets have had time to come in (about 7 days), and new damage you mark keeps it held.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">The closing copy of both rental agreements follows by itself: time and date in, kilometres in, driven and charged, fuel in, the hours late, the new damage, the return charges and the totals, countersigned with your name, emailed to the renter.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>New damage needs a close-up photo and a clear note. Finance uses your photos and notes to bill the renter, so take your time.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>If the renter already pressed I&#39;ve returned the car, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">The renter says the car is back</b> with their photos and readings. Check the car in as usual: that completes the trip and settles their report.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-return-on-one-screen-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">On one screen (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">The check-in is one screen too: the actual return time (late charges follow it), km, fuel, photos and a note. A renter who returned the car themselves with km, fuel and photos has already completed the trip; add photos if anything is missing.</p></section>');
